Substantive changes from upstream:

  - Crate names rebranded to remove the "Inferno" identity from
    user-visible surfaces:
      * inferno_aoip          → sonusgrid_engine        (in `aoip/`)
      * alsa_pcm_inferno      → sonusgrid_alsa_plugin   (in `alsa-plugin/`)
      * inferno2pipe          → sonusgrid_pipe          (in `sonusgrid-pipe/`)
  - mDNS TXT record `mf` field changed from "Inferno-AoIP" to "SonusGrid".
  - State directory moved from `~/.local/state/inferno_aoip/` to
    `~/.local/state/sonusgrid/`.
  - ALSA plugin output renamed:
      libasound_module_pcm_inferno.so → libasound_module_pcm_sonusgrid.so
    Plugin entry symbol renamed from `_snd_pcm_inferno_open` to
    `_snd_pcm_sonusgrid_open`.
  - Channel friendly_names default to numeric form ("01", "02", …)
    instead of "TX 1"/"RX 1".

The mDNS sub-crate `searchfire` (in this workspace) is itself a fork by
the upstream Inferno author of WilliamVenner's `searchlight` crate. It
is preserved here at its upstream layout to make merges from teodly's
upstream tree straightforward.

The `alsa-sys-all` and `usrvclock-rs` sub-crates are kept verbatim from
upstream; they are infrastructure (FFI bindings; unix-socket helper) and
have nothing Inferno-specific in them.

